## Automatic calculations

Calculate the nutrition totals for the selected date from saved food entries.

Use this logic:

Consumed calories = sum of calories for all food items logged that day.

Consumed protein = sum of protein across all logged items.

Consumed carbohydrates = sum of carbohydrates across all logged items.

Consumed fat = sum of fat across all logged items.

Remaining calories = daily calorie target minus consumed calories.

Remaining macronutrients = target minus consumed quantity.

If a target has been exceeded, clearly show the excess rather than displaying a negative value as remaining nutrition.

Retain the actual consumed value in all cases.

Do not confuse remaining calories with the calories in an individual food.

