### Nutrition calculation tests

Verify that:

- 50 g of a food with 200 kcal per 100 g calculates to 100 kcal.
- 150 g of a food with 10 g protein per 100 g calculates to 15 g protein.
- Combining two foods sums their nutrients correctly.
- Changing serving quantity updates all totals.
- Removing a food subtracts its contribution.
- Editing a meal does not corrupt historical logs.
- A food with zero calories can still have a valid record if the data source supports it.
- Missing nutritional values are handled explicitly rather than silently treated as verified zeros.

Use appropriate rounding for display.

Preserve adequate precision internally.

